WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.700
 Thank you Sam. We have been pretty friends for over 45 years so you'll have to

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.580
 excuse to have

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:23.750
 heard of it. Sam and I are really our friends because we're both in love with

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:31.580
 the same woman, my mother. We call her every day.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:40.990
 And the things that Sam said were true and I had to give that judgment to you.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:46.480
 It's because I am the son of George and Lee Pricklow,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:55.380
 two Italian immigrants. I'm very proud of my ethnic tradition and I'm happy it's

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.780
 represented here.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.800
 You know Cleveland is the best argument against the melting pot here. Nothing

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.780
 ever melted. Nothing ever melted.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:20.380
 And what a blessing. What a blessing it has been that nothing melted. Diversity

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:25.780
 usually is put into context of a challenge or a problem

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:34.030
 that has not been my experience. Diversity is a gift. An example of the beauty

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.780
 of my point of view of the infinite beauty of God's

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:50.780
 how it reflected the lives and humanity in all of the persons.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:02:03.660
 You know friends, contemporary society has its own standards for judging a

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.780
 person's success.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:14.910
 But I just want to say this evening nothing of what the world calls success

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:21.780
 from my perspective, nothing can begin to compare with the

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:30.880
 grace filled experiences I've had administering to the people of this community,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:40.780
 all the people of this community and especially the Catholic community.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:48.290
 I should be thanking you and the people of this community. What a privilege and

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:53.780
 an honor it was to be in your midst. This city has wonderful people,

00:02:53.780 --> 00:03:00.770
 wonderful people, generous people, compassionate people and we need to raise

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:05.780
 that up. That's why I think evenings like tonight are so important.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:15.780
 What an honor it is to be part of this day with the good people that are here.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:24.020
 The greatest reward I had was working with the people and I had the great

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.780
 privilege and honor of working with people at the

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:36.380
 diocesan staff, tremendously talented people. All the things that people say I

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:40.780
 did, anybody who has been in an executive position know we did the name.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:45.770
 But it's the people that will work with us to do the work and I had the

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:52.200
 blessing of being associated with some wonderful, wonderful people who were so

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:52.780
 talented.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:58.780
 I'm a history teacher and I always remember Van Newkran

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.990
 If you want to be successful, hire people who are smarter than you are and let

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:02.780
 them do their job.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:08.780
 Let them do their job.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:16.410
 And you did a wonderful job. It was such a privilege, such a privilege to be

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:17.780
 able to do there.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:25.540
 I can't tell you the satisfaction that comes from the ministry to you good

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.780
 people.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:36.370
 Retirement is wonderful. There's a lot about being a bishop, but I'm happy it's

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.780
 in the next.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:43.060
 But the thing that I miss most is the people, the great people of this

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:49.350
 community and we need to work together to keep this community what it has been

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:49.780
 and can't be.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:56.630
 And it's people who are going to do it. People who respect each other, love one

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.780
 another and know one another.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:08.580
 If we do that, there's not much we can't do. That kind of satisfaction working

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:15.720
 in that has been far better than any prominent, efficient position or any cause

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.780
 of the people.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:23.780
 So I thank you for the privilege of being part of this community in my ministry.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.780
 God bless you all.

